Native CT thermomagnetic spacecraft diagnostic (Codex-solver)

Existing completed CT probes only. Physical geometric UTC, Nov25 onward; native hourly windows exactly reuse observations/analyze_native_model.py. Model Tp uses total-fluid p=2 np kB Tp under Te=Tp. This is not an independently evolved electron/proton temperature comparison. Derive Tp and scalar |B| first, then average; do not form them from averaged components. No fitted phase/amplitude, recalibration, reference selection, Parker remap, forward run, or chart.

Fieldwise finite-positive masks and complete-hour coverage are explicit in every TSV row and JSON count. All four cases retain 235 Wind / 240 STEREO-A / 235 Solar Orbiter paired hours for both fields; future/missing coverage is rejected rather than extrapolated. The validation period starts after the normalization-training stop; Wind is also excluded from training as an instrument.

